{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1435 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "79bee7281fedddab8255697533c5802aeb6e760968ee98d1632177d75dd295f2" :edb/db-before-t 1434 :edb/db-after-t 1435 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534747 50 #inst "2026-10-12T10:24:30.531Z" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186122084 1075 #edb/ref 17592186122085 13194139534747 17592186045417 false] [17592186122084 1075 #edb/ref 17592186122086 13194139534747 17592186045417 false] [17592186122084 1075 #edb/ref 17592186122087 13194139534747 17592186045417 false] [17592186122084 1075 #edb/ref 17592186122088 13194139534747 17592186045417 false] [17592186122084 1075 #edb/ref 17592186122089 13194139534747 17592186045417 false] [17592186122084 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434935 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186122084 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434940 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186122084 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434944 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186122084 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434946 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186122084 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434947 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186122084 1078 #edb/ref 17592186434944 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186124492 1038 #edb/ref 17592186434950 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186124494 1038 #edb/ref 17592186434951 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186124914 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186124914 1071 "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $B$ to the basis $C$ is given by\n$P_{B → C} = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 9\\end{bmatrix}$.\nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$." 13194139534747 17592186045417 false] [17592186124914 1071 "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $B$ to the basis $C$ is given by \n${P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 9\\end{aligned}].$\nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$  ." 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186124914 1074 "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 9\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 9-(-5)\\cdot (-6)}[\\begin{aligned}9 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-3}[\\begin{aligned}9 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186323799 1071 "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ and $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$ be bases of ${R}^{2}.$ If ${b}_{1}=5{c}_{2}-3{c}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}=2{c}_{1}-4{c}_{2},$ find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to C}$ from $B$ to $C.$" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186323799 1071 "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ and $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$ be bases of ${R}^{2}.$ If ${b}_{1}=5{c}_{2}-3{c}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}=2{c}_{1}-4{c}_{2},$ find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to C}$ from $B$ to $C.$" 13194139534747 17592186045417 false] [17592186377851 1071 "Let $B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]\\}$  be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{2}.$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $S$ to $B.$" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186377851 1071 "Let $B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]}$  be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{2}.$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $S$ to $B.$" 13194139534747 17592186045417 false] [17592186377851 1074 "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $S$ as $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ and $\\{{e}_{1},{e}_{2}\\}$, respectively. Recall that the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$ consists of the vectors\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{e}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $S$ to $B$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $S$ relative to the basis $B.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${e}_{1}$ and ${e}_{2}$ relative to the basis $B.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & {e}_{1} & {e}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we simply reduce the left-hand side to reduced row-echelon form using Gaussian elimination: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 11 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 11 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the right-hand side, we obtain the change-of-coordinates matrix from $S$ to $B.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{S\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}11 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186377851 1074 "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $S$ as ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ and ${{e}_{1},{e}_{2}}$, respectively. Recall that the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$ consists of the vectors\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{e}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $S$ to $B$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $S$ relative to the basis $B.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${e}_{1}$ and ${e}_{2}$ relative to the basis $B.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & {e}_{1} & {e}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we simply reduce the left-hand side to reduced row-echelon form using Gaussian elimination: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 11 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 11 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the right-hand side, we obtain the change-of-coordinates matrix from $S$ to $B.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{S\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}11 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534747 17592186045417 false] [17592186394291 1071 "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{2}.$ \nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to S}$ from $B$ to $S$ if \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186394291 1071 "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{2}.$ \nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to S}$ from $B$ to $S$ if \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534747 17592186045417 false] [17592186416596 1071 "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ and $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}\\}$ be bases of ${R}^{3}.$ \nWhat are the values of $a,b,$ and $c$ if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & =2{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}+{c}_{3}, \\\\ {b}_{2} & =4{c}_{1}-2{c}_{3}, \\\\ {b}_{3} & =2{c}_{1}-3{c}_{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand  the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & a & 2 \\\\ b & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & c & -3\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186416596 1071 "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ and $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}}$ be bases of ${R}^{3}.$ \nWhat are the values of $a,b,$ and $c$ if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & =2{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}+{c}_{3}, \\\\ {b}_{2} & =4{c}_{1}-2{c}_{3}, \\\\ {b}_{3} & =2{c}_{1}-3{c}_{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand  the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & a & 2 \\\\ b & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & c & -3\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" 13194139534747 17592186045417 false] [17592186434934 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434934 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434934 1083 #uuid "16bee97f-7038-5e53-805e-c034d4f9aa98" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434935 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434935 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434935 1083 #uuid "20f58787-8399-5ca4-a011-8a6df79512f1" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434936 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434936 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434936 1083 #uuid "344c3b89-889a-5113-860d-9f442b0f7b5f" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434937 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434937 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434937 1083 #uuid "53b1d470-247b-548b-b13d-bc66e9449c39" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434938 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434938 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434938 1083 #uuid "7251156a-c21f-5adb-9ff9-bd33a768f1d5" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434939 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434939 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434939 1083 #uuid "753fb253-4ce3-57c6-9f54-6bb8fae24d9a" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434940