5fe-6463-5cf0-bb39-9946f196f0dc" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434947 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434947 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434947 1083 #uuid "ef95b44c-9f4a-5eb2-8a32-5755e8f3f15d" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434948 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434936 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434948 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434939 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434948 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434941 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434948 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434942 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434948 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434945 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434948 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434948 1077 "selection" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434948 1078 #edb/ref 17592186434942 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434948 1079 #uuid "0710a289-e926-5692-b8d2-c99ac59e739f" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434949 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434934 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434949 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434937 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434949 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434938 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434949 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434943 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434949 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434949 1077 "selection" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434949 1078 #edb/ref 17592186434937 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434949 1079 #uuid "99aa8a6d-990b-5e61-8b84-2888eb56d9f3" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434950 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434949 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434950 1069 "q-113116" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434950 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434950 1071 "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{2}.$ \nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to S}$ from $B$ to $S$ if \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434950 1072 #uuid "75d038ad-b39f-5c52-a2ee-ada0d3f5df01" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434950 1074 "Recall  that the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$ consists of the vectors ${e}_{1}$ and ${e}_{2},$ given by\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{e}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe components of the vectors of $B$ are just the coordinates relative to the standard basis:\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,[{b}_{2}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $S.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434951 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434948 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434951 1069 "q-113519" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434951 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434951 1071 "Let $B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}$ and $C=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\}$ be bases of ${R}^{2}.$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434951 1072 #uuid "f9a03134-8525-58b4-a224-da8d571c355f" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true] [17592186434951 1074 "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $C$ as $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ and $\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$, respectively.\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ relative to the basis $C.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we simply reduce the left-hand side to reduced row-echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -8 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-4){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the right-hand side, we obtain the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534747 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-16bee97f-7038-5e53-805e-c034d4f9aa98" 17592186434934 "answer-20f58787-8399-5ca4-a011-8a6df79512f1" 17592186434935 "answer-344c3b89-889a-5113-860d-9f442b0f7b5f" 17592186434936 "answer-53b1d470-247b-548b-b13d-bc66e9449c39" 17592186434937 "answer-7251156a-c21f-5adb-9ff9-bd33a768f1d5" 17592186434938 "answer-753fb253-4ce3-57c6-9f54-6bb8fae24d9a" 17592186434939 "answer-91a0872a-5de1-5bcf-bf96-cd7b7f09e1c4" 17592186434940 "answer-a20fd614-e995-59f1-8191-fd45b0182f75" 17592186434941 "answer-a2788a1d-e2ab-584c-86fe-21bbcb38e3ab" 17592186434942 "answer-bdb98ddb-73a6-5232-b35f-26201c89674c" 17592186434943 "answer-c3bfcb95-4180-5b13-9c4f-4eca7f2802a4" 17592186434944 "answer-c8e82d70-a589-5d2a-9e35-2278a91f4109" 17592186434945 "answer-da5b45fe-6463-5cf0-bb39-9946f196f0dc" 17592186434946 "answer